.PP
Stringification refers to the \f[CR]#\f[R] operator in macros, used to
convert pure inputs to strings.
.PP
Example:
.IP
.EX
#define X(A) #A

printf( X( i am testing something ) ); \f[I]// Will return: \(dqi am testing something\(dq without a new line.\f[R]
